<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nanyadeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1097</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nanyadeva was the founder of the Karnat dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithila">Mithila</a>, establishing himself in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirhut">Tirhut</a> plain of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> around 1097. A chief of Karnata origin, he probably came north with the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of Kalyani, and he made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simraungadh">Simraungadh</a> his capital. His dynasty ruled Mithila until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>'s invasion of 1324.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nanyadeva.jpg" alt="Nanyadeva" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nanyadeva · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Image_of_a_horseman_from_12th_century_land_grant_of_Nanyadeva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
